    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's not just a symptom though. it's a reality. no amount of therapy is going to stop the cells from dying or fix the gaps in my memory. i just feel like i'm fighting a losing battle against time. there’s a certain kind of dignity in being able to say goodbye while i still have my wits about me. like, wouldn't it make more sense to choose how the story ends instead of just waiting for the blank pages to take over?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
